            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0429" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">57013/1.</note>
                <head>Her Majesty’s Treasury to Laird Brothers.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Chambers,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> In reply to your letter of the 12th
                    instant, proposing that the El Tousson and El Monnassir should be placed in the
                    Birkenhead docks, and there completed, I am commanded by the lords commissioners
                    of her Majesty’s treasury to inform you that their lordships regret that they
                    are unable to comply with your request.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. A. HAMILTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird</hi> &amp; Co., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Birkenhead.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
